# candidate: connectome-host 0.21.0, agent-framework 0.32.0, context-manager 0.24.0, membrane 0.8.0, chronicle 0.5.1, bun 1.4.4
templates
T:call-a-quiet-stretch = (A quiet stretch: # messages of routine system traffic — heartbeats, empty turns, notices. Nothing happened worth remembering.)
T:call-clock-tuesday-#-#-# = Clock: Tuesday #-#-#, #:# UTC
T:call-context-manager-cm-recall = Context Manager: [CM] Recall memory L#-#.
T:call-context-manager-cm-the = Context Manager: [CM] The conversation resumes.
T:call-context-manager-system = Context Manager: System: You will soon form a new memory, get ready. The messages that follow are the slice of recent experience you are about to compress. After them, write the memory in your own voice.
T:call-context-manager-topic = Context Manager: [Topic Transition]
  
  A new topic.
T:call-context-manager-write-the-memory-of-events = Context Manager: Write the memory of events since the most recent memory system notification. Speak in the first person from your own perspective. Preserve concrete details — file paths, exact values, decisions, unresolved questions, the user's active asks. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no section headers unless they help preservation, no meta-commentary about summarizing. Memorize only what actually happened in that slice: if it holds little beyond routine system traffic (heartbeats, empty turns, failure notices), a short memory saying so is correct — do not pad it by re-narrating events you already remember from earlier as if they had just happened again.
T:call-context-manager-write-the-memory-of-this = Context Manager: Write the memory of this slice of the log. This part of the record predates your own first turn: it is inherited context you carry — others' lived experience, witnessed through the log, not your own. Attribute events to the participants named in the record ("Ash and Tavy explored...", "the log holds...", "before my arrival..."), and reserve the first person for your own reading of it: what stood out to you, what it means to carry this. Preserve concrete details — names, decisions, exact phrases that matter, unresolved questions. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no meta-commentary about summarizing.
  
  This stretch is a record you inherited, not your own experience.
T:call-context-manager-you-have-just-reviewed-the-l# = Context Manager: You have just reviewed the L# memories above, in chronological order. They cover the stretch of experience you are about to consolidate into a single L# memory. Write a memory that preserves the through-line: what happened, what was decided, what remains open, what concrete details future you will want to reach for. Speak in the first person. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no meta-commentary about summarizing.
T:call-context-manager-you-have-just-reviewed-the-slices = Context Manager: You have just reviewed the slices of recent experience above (raw conversation), in chronological order. They cover the stretch of experience you are about to consolidate into a single L# memory. Write a memory that preserves the through-line: what happened, what was decided, what remains open, what concrete details future you will want to reach for. Speak in the first person. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no meta-commentary about summarizing.
T:call-empty = 
  
  ---
  
  
T:call-routing-your-plain = [routing] Your plain speech now lands in chat. Other channels need an explicit send tool.
T:call-the-local-time = The local time at the start of this session is #-#-#T#:#:#.#+#:# [UTC].
T:call-user-clock-monday = user: Clock: Monday #-#-#, #:# UTC
T:call-user-delivered-plain = user: [delivered] plain speech → chat
T:context-manager-recall-l#-# = [Recall L#-#]
T:context-manager-topic-transition-a = [Topic Transition]
  
  A new topic.
